The slurp loader directly searches the DECtape logical drive units using passed file parameters of the starting block and logical unit for all input files passed to the BIN program.  When the proper starting block is located, the program is directly loaded into memory using the novel technique of using a one-word buffer within the slurp loader.\cf2   The slurp loader applies to other than just DECtapes, so should you state that it "... searches the ___ device logical drive units..."?  I forget the term that ought to be in the "___".\line\line\cf3 No, each device has a different slurp loader, only the format is the same, the methods are generally analogous, never identical.  The notion of searching only applies to DECtapes and LINC-8 LINCtapes.  The search operation is intrinsically in the hardware on the PDP-12 and why that slurp loader is the only one with a restriction:\line\line a) You are not allowed to load into 07400-07577.  It's a buffer for the TC12 slurp loader which is read after being read in not overlapping as in all the other three cases.\line\line b) If you need to load your program into 07400-07577, use the virtual loader /V option, then no restrictions, but it will write on the drive.\line\line The RX devices don't search but they have two operations, one to get the desired sector into the buffer, and another to unload the buffer a word at a time, all by program transfer, so timing is moot, all asynchronous.  Writing is load the buffer and then write the buffer, so all read or write operations have to do two of the four operations, etc.\line\line Everything else is just a read or a write.\line\line So, this is a TC01/TC08 detail only. Each slurp loader has its own problems and solutions, again only sharing the file format, which is the main thrust of this document.\par
